---
// The two install dialogs: "How to install" and "macOS blocked Slinky". On every page with a Download button,
// since the first launch needs Open Anyway until Slinky is notarized.
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import OpenAnyway from './OpenAnyway.astro';
import release from '../release.json';
---
  <div class="modal" data-help role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="help-title">
    <div class="modal__box">
      <button class="modal__close" type="button" data-close-help aria-label="Close">×</button>
      <h3 id="help-title">macOS blocked Slinky</h3>
      <p class="modal__lead">Slinky isn’t notarized yet, so macOS stops the first launch. Open <b>System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security</b>, scroll down to <b>Security</b> and click <b>Open Anyway</b>, then confirm with Touch ID or your password. You only do this once.</p>
      <OpenAnyway />
      <p class="modal__note">No Open Anyway button? Paste this into Terminal:</p>
      <div class="cmd"><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Slinky.app</code><button type="button" data-copy-cmd>Copy</button></div>
      <p class="modal__note">A slash through the icon means this Mac can’t run Slinky. It needs Apple silicon.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="modal" data-install role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="modal__box">
      <button class="modal__close" type="button" data-close-install aria-label="Close">×</button>
      <h3 id="install-title">How to install Slinky</h3>
      <p class="modal__lead">Both put Slinky in Applications. Needs an <b>Apple silicon</b> Mac with {release.minOS} or later.</p>
      <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Install method">
        <button role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="dmg" type="button">Download &amp; install</button>
        <button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="brew" type="button">Homebrew</button>
      </div>
      <div data-panel="dmg">
        <ol>
          <li>Open <b>Slinky-{release.version}.dmg</b> and drag Slinky into Applications. <span class="modal__fallback">Download didn’t start? <a href={release.dmg} data-track="Download macOS install-fallback">Download again</a>.</span></li>
          <li>Open Slinky. Since it isn’t notarized yet, macOS stops it once: open <b>System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security</b>, scroll down to <b>Security</b> and click <b>Open Anyway</b>, then confirm with Touch ID or your password.<OpenAnyway /></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="modal__note">Still blocked? Paste this into Terminal:</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Slinky.app</code><button type="button" data-copy-cmd>Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div data-panel="brew" hidden>
        <p class="modal__note">With <a href="https://brew.sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Homebrew</a>, add the tap once, then install:</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>brew tap heyderekj/slinky https://github.com/heyderekj/slinky</code><button type="button" data-copy-cmd>Copy</button></div>
        <div class="cmd"><code>brew install --cask slinky</code><button type="button" data-copy-cmd>Copy</button></div>
        <p class="modal__note">Upgrade later with <code>brew upgrade --cask slinky</code>. If macOS blocks the first launch, use <b>Open Anyway</b> as in step 2 of Download &amp; install.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="modal__callout"><Icon name="update" /><p><b>Updates in place.</b> One click checks for new releases, and only installs ones signed by Slinky’s developer.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
